.DS_Store
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Reference material used while building: the companion China map and the
# course timelines the place list was drawn from. Not part of this project,
# and not mine to republish.
inspiration/

# The two OSM coastline extracts the fine-detail layer is built from: 11 MB and
# 44 MB of survey-grade coastline, of which the map can draw about one part in
# twenty. tools/trim_fine_sources.py cuts them down to the *-islands.geojson
# files beside them, and those are what is committed and what the build reads.
tools/cache/japanese-home-islands.geojson
tools/cache/pacific-islands-se.geojson
tools/cache/*.qmd

# The computed frontier seams, kept so a build that changes nothing about the
# geometry does not spend three seconds working them out again. Derived, keyed
# on a hash of the geometry and of the code that made them, and rewritten
# whenever either changes — so there is nothing here worth a place in history.
tools/cache/seams-*.json

# GeoJSON written by `python3 tools/build_map.py --export exports` — the map's
# own geometry in lon/lat, for opening in QGIS. Regenerated on demand, and far
# too heavy to keep in the history.
exports/

# The GeoNames bulk, 588 MB of it, all in one place so that what is ignored
# under data/ is a directory rather than three patterns: 2.7 million populated
# places as tab-separated country dumps, the global cities500 file, the 201 MB
# full-detail China GeoJSON, and the four working layers built from them.
#
# None of it is read by any build step. cities-gaz.js comes from
# data/cities-1930.csv and data/cities-1942.csv; the gazetteer was the pool the
# 446 cities were chosen from, and the choosing is done. What is committed is
# the recipe — data/gazetteer/README.md and build_geojson.py — and whoever
# needs the layers rebuilds them into data/ignored/ from the dumps.
data/ignored/

# Working scratch, not part of the map. rr.html is a saved copy of somebody
# else's site kept while looking at how they model historical boundaries;
# whg.tmp is a zero-byte leftover; deletion-tests holds a copy of a superseded
# occupied-zone file kept while testing what the removal tool did to it.
stale/rr.html
stale/whg.tmp
tools/cache/deletion-tests/

# The texts editor: a local tool for browsing and editing everything under
# texts/, and the zip snapshots it takes before every save. It edits the files
# that are committed; it is not one of them.
texts/admin/

# Puppeteer, for tools/compare_perf.js and the headless checks. 300 MB, and
# nothing the map ships needs it: install it here when you want to measure
# something and leave it out of the history.
node_modules/

# screenshots the annotation tests write beside themselves
/a-*.png
/lay-*.png
/arrow.png
/arrow-tips.png
/symsheet.png
/locked.png
/three*.png
